The draft needs a stronger evidence shape: a closed `¬ ...` theorem can show only that an input is invalid. There’s also a logical constraint: if a planted witness satisfies every premise and falsifies the conclusion of the unchanged law, it contradicts that law. The convention needs an explicit mutation mapping and a check that the witness uses the law’s conclusion with that mutation.

The existing axiom inventory includes generated theorems, so the gate also needs to distinguish authored laws from generated declarations using the shared population.
